    "options": {
      "A": "After inserting $15$, the sorted list is $5$, $7$, $9$, $11$, $13$, $15$; the middle pair is $9$ and $11$, so the median becomes $10$.",
      "B": "Say the median moves after inserting $15$, skipping that the list must stay sorted and the new middle position(s) must be checked.",
      "C": "The median moves upward because $15$ is greater than the earlier median $9$.",
      "D": "Use the same middle-tracking rule to decide how the mean changes when $15$ is inserted."
